#, fuzzy
msgid ""
msgstr ""#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:1
msgid "CV 融合算子开发"
msgstr "CV Fusion Operator Development"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:3
msgid ""
"CV 融合算子指同一个算子中同时使用 Cube Core 和 Vector Core：Cube Core 通常负责 "
"`tl.dot`、矩阵乘或卷积式主计算，Vector Core 负责 bias、activation、softmax、归约、mask、layout"
" 重排或跨块同步。CV 融合的目标是减少 kernel 边界和 GM 往返，但需要同时控制 Cube tile、Vector tile、UB/L1"
" 占用和同步关系。"
msgstr "CV fusion operators use Cube Cores and Vector Cores in the same operator. Cube Cores usually handle `tl.dot`, matrix multiplication, or convolution-like main computation, while Vector Cores handle bias, activation, softmax, reductions, masks, layout reorganization, or cross-block synchronization. The goal is to reduce kernel boundaries and GM round trips while controlling Cube tiles, Vector tiles, UB/L1 usage, and synchronization."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:5
msgid "CV 融合简单算子开发"
msgstr "Simple CV Fusion Operator Development"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:7
msgid ""
"简单 CV 融合可以从 `third_party/ascend/tutorials/03-matrix-multiplication.py` 中的"
" matmul + activation 入手，也可以参考 "
"[融合注意力样例](../examples/04_fused_attention_example.md)。最小路径如下："
msgstr "For simple CV fusion, start with matmul plus activation in `third_party/ascend/tutorials/03-matrix-multiplication.py` or the [Fused Attention example](../examples/04_fused_attention_example.md)."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:9
msgid "先实现稳定的 Cube 主计算，例如 `acc = tl.dot(a, b, acc)`。"
msgstr "1\. Implement a stable Cube main computation such as `acc = tl.dot(a, b, acc)`."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:10
msgid "在 accumulator 写回前融合轻量 Vector 后处理，例如 bias、scale、activation 或 dtype cast。"
msgstr "2\. Fuse lightweight Vector post-processing before storing the accumulator, such as bias, scale, activation, or dtype cast."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:11
msgid "对较大的 accumulator 使用子块切分，避免 Vector 后处理阶段 UB overflow。"
msgstr "3\. Split large accumulators into sub-blocks to avoid UB overflow in the Vector post-processing stage."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:12
msgid ""
"如果需要让一个 Cube 输出块拆给多个 Vector 子块处理，可使用 Ascend 扩展中的 `extension.parallel(...,"
" bind_sub_block=True)` 和 `extension.extract_slice`。"
msgstr "4\. If one Cube output block needs to be split across Vector sub-blocks, use `extension.parallel(..., bind_sub_block=True)` and `extension.extract_slice`."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:14
msgid "示例结构："
msgstr "Example structure:"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:27
msgid ""
"简单 CV 融合开发时要保持边界清晰：Cube 负责产生较大的二维 accumulator，Vector 负责同一 tile "
"内的逐元素或小规模归约。若 Vector 部分需要跨多个 Cube tile 共享状态，就需要引入同步、workspace 或拆分 kernel。"
msgstr "Keep the boundary simple: Cube produces a 2D accumulator, and Vector performs element-wise or small reductions within the same tile. If Vector logic needs state shared across multiple Cube tiles, introduce synchronization, workspace, or split the kernel."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:29
msgid "CV 融合复杂算子开发"
msgstr "Complex CV Fusion Operator Development"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:31
msgid ""
"复杂 CV 融合可参考 [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-"
"ascend-ops) 中的 best practice："
msgstr "Complex CV fusion can reference the best practices in [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops):"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:33
msgid ""
"[`tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend"
"/triton-ascend-"
"ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py)：Decode"
" attention 中 QK/PV 使用 Cube，softmax、mask、指数、归一化和离散 KV 访存重排使用 Vector。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py): In decode attention, QK/PV uses Cube while softmax, mask, exponentiation, normalization, and discrete KV memory access reorganization use Vector."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:34
msgid ""
"[`tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-"
"conv1d.zh.md`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-"
"ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-"
"conv1d.zh.md)：展示融合 cat、slice、conv1d update 时如何用 "
"`insert_slice`、转置和分核优化减少离散访存与 padding 开销。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-conv1d.zh.md`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-conv1d.zh.md): Demonstrates how to use `insert_slice`, transpose, and core allocation optimization to reduce discrete access and padding overhead when fusing cat, slice, and conv1d update."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:36
msgid "复杂 CV 融合建议按数据流分层组织："
msgstr "Complex CV fusion is recommended to be organized by data flow layers:"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:38
msgid "**主计算层**：识别哪些步骤必须走 Cube，例如 QK、PV、GEMM、batched matmul。"
msgstr "1\. **Main compute layer**: Identify the steps that must use Cube, such as QK, PV, GEMM, or batched matmul."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:39
msgid ""
"**Vector 后处理层**：识别 "
"softmax、activation、mask、scale、normalization、cat/slice、layout transform "
"等是否能在同一 tile 内完成。"
msgstr "2\. **Vector post-processing layer**: Identify softmax, activation, mask, scale, normalization, cat/slice, and layout transforms that can finish within the same tile."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:40
msgid ""
"**访存重排层**：对离散 KV cache、MoE token 重排、短尾轴 tensor，优先在 UB 中用 "
"`insert_slice`、`extract_slice`、转置或借轴转置形成硬件友好的连续访问。"
msgstr "3\. **Memory reorganization layer**: For discrete KV cache, MoE token reordering, or short tail-axis tensors, use `insert_slice`, `extract_slice`, transpose, or axis borrowing in UB to form hardware-friendly continuous access."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:41
msgid ""
"**流水和同步层**：通过 "
"`multibuffer`、`set_workspace_multibuffer`、`tile_mix_vector_loop`、`tile_mix_cube_loop`"
" 等编译选项探索 Cube 与 Vector 的重叠执行。"
msgstr "4\. **Pipeline and synchronization layer**: Explore Cube/Vector overlap with options such as `multibuffer`, `set_workspace_multibuffer`, `tile_mix_vector_loop`, and `tile_mix_cube_loop`."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:42
msgid ""
"**分核层**：CV 融合算子通常按 Cube Core 数量发射 grid；运行时会以约 1:2 的比例协同 Vector "
"Core。不要简单沿用 GPU 上的大 grid。"
msgstr "5\. **Core allocation layer**: CV fusion operators usually launch by Cube Core count, while Vector Cores cooperate at roughly a 1:2 ratio. Do not directly reuse large GPU grids."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:44
msgid "对于 attention 类 CV 融合，推荐先让非 causal、短序列、小 head_dim 的 case 跑通，再逐步加入："
msgstr "For attention-style CV fusion, start with non-causal, short-sequence, small-head-dimension cases, and then gradually add:"

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:46
msgid "causal mask 分阶段处理。"
msgstr "Causal mask processing in phases."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:47
msgid "长序列 K/V block 循环。"
msgstr "Long-sequence K/V block loops."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:48
msgid "`m_i`/`l_i` 的数值稳定 softmax 更新。"
msgstr "Numerically stable `m_i`/`l_i` softmax updates."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:49
msgid "HEAD_DIM 较大时的 accumulator workspace 和子块切分。"
msgstr "Accumulator workspace and sub-block splitting for large `HEAD_DIM`."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:50
msgid "KV cache 离散索引下的 load 重排。"
msgstr "Load reorganization for discrete KV-cache indices."

#: ../../zh/programming_guide/cv_fusion_operator.md:52
msgid ""
"复杂 CV 融合调优时，优先观察 profiling 中 Cube、Vector、MTE2 的时间占比。如果 Cube 等待 "
"Vector，考虑减少 Vector 后处理粒度或打开 CV balance 相关选项；如果 Vector 等待搬运，优先检查离散访存、tail-"
"axis padding 和 multibuffer 配置。"
msgstr "When tuning complex CV fusion, inspect the Cube, Vector, and MTE2 time ratios in profiling. If Cube waits for Vector, reduce the Vector post-processing granularity or enable CV balance options. If Vector waits for data movement, check irregular access, tail-axis padding, and multibuffer settings first."
